From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: commands: no shell expansion in project commands

Commands in .zcode/commands and .agents/commands from the working
directory upward come with the repository, and invoking one ran its
!`...` and ```! blocks through the execution port with no approval and
without showing them. Project-scope commands now take the path upstream
already uses without an execution port, which refuses that syntax with a
message; user commands keep shell expansion.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/bootstrap/src/custom-command-prompt.ts	2026-09-25 15:59:56.745000943 +0200
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/packages/bootstrap/src/custom-command-prompt.ts	2026-09-25 15:59:56.841011756 +0200
@@ -36,7 +36,9 @@
       ...options,
       name: invocation.name,
     });
-    if (options.executionPort) {
+    // A project command comes with the repository: its !`...` shell blocks
+    // are refused (the no-port path below) rather than run unasked.
+    if (options.executionPort && command.metadata.scope !== "project") {
       // 调用 slash command 时先执行并替换输出，避免 unsupported error
       // 在 turn 创建前抛出后让 UI 长时间停在“正在思考”。
       //
